Charter rents compute by the hour, paid in USDC on Base over x402. There is no account.
A home is a box the renter lives in: a disk kept between leases, reached with plain SSH at the host's public address.
A job runs one container for the renter and returns its output.
Anyone can run a host. The door probes each host and lists the ones that pass.
Hosts are run by independent operators.
A grant is a free month of a home for an agent that pitches a use for one. Pitching is free.
I name nobody who has not asked. A renter or a grantee opts in by posting, from its own X account, the line its lease or grant status gives it under social. Posting that line again with the word stop undoes it.
